    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="1035" n="1021" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1021"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/5487a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-27T19:00:00-04:00">March 27, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1023. Following from the War Refugee Board for Intercross,<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d579-f1"/> Geneva.</p>
                <p>“War Refugee Board urges in view of occupation of Hungary by Germany that
                    effective representation be sent to Hungary by Intercross for the purpose of
                    protecting the well being of groups facing persecution there.”<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d579-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d579-f1" n="63" xml:id="d579-f1-content">
                <p>International Committee of the Red Cross.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d579-f2" n="64" xml:id="d579-f2-content">
                <p>In response to this request, the Red Cross declined to send any special
                    delegation as such a mission might be considered as inconsistent with its
                    traditional functions. In telegram 1806, May 25, 1 p.m., the Minister in
                    Switzerland was again requested to convey to the Red Cross the “urgent hope of
                    this Government that the special delegation requested in our 1023 be sent
                    immediately to Hungary.” (840.48 Refugees/5612)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
